  "handoff": {
    "summary": "M4RI and igraph dependency stamps are now canonical receipts that bind the pinned source, target ABI and deployment, complete portable/cpu-native policy, build flags, actual build toolchain, public interface header, and every installed output byte. Their worktree-cache identities now vary with the complete mathematics profile. Portable M4RI uses fixed conservative cache geometry instead of embedding the builder CPU's detected cache sizes; cpu-native retains detection and is CPU-fingerprinted.",
    "risks": [
      "Generated adapter manifests do not yet name their dependency receipt. SEA integration must explicitly map each embedded adapter to its corresponding dependency receipt rather than treating two independent hashes as provenance.",
      "Static archives can still contain compiler source paths. Exact output receipts expose this drift but deterministic prefix-map flags are a separate reproducible-build follow-up.",
      "The new receipts require fresh M4RI and igraph prefixes on every release platform; legacy stamps intentionally fail closed and rebuild."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Embed and validate the M4RI and igraph receipts in the SEA build manifest, requiring their math profile fingerprints to match FLINT and FFLAS.",
      "Bind every generated FFI manifest and base addon to its dependency receipt/profile in the release receipt.",
      "Rebuild on Linux x64, macOS arm64, Linux arm64, and Windows x64 and retain platform validation receipts."
    ]
  }
